cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MLatelier in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MLatelier: A Zero-Code Multi-Modal Machine Learning Workshop with Integrated Explainability"
abstract: >-
  MLatelier is a browser-based Streamlit application that lets users without
  programming experience run complete machine learning experiments across
  tabular, vision, and text data. It combines Bayesian hyperparameter
  optimisation over 20+ scikit-learn-compatible estimators and twelve
  pre-trained vision architectures with built-in explainability (SHAP, LIME, partial
  dependence plots, Grad-CAM), a configurable ablation module, and multi-label
  classification support.
type: software
